        "original_id": "e802334d-58f8-5471-a8c9-408063dd9b08",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Joseph L. Mankiewicz, Tony Kaye, Laurence Fishburne, Karl Urban\n- Roles: film director, screenwriter, producer\n- Awards: Academy Awards for Best Director, Best Writing, Screenplay\n- Works: A Letter to Three Wives, All About Eve, Black Water Transit\n- Topics: Hollywood careers, film and documentary directing\n\nFacts:\n- Joseph L. Mankiewicz was born on February 11, 1909, and he was an American film director, screenwriter, and producer.\n- Joseph L. Mankiewicz won the Academy Award for Best Director and the Academy Award for Best Writing, Screenplay for A Letter to Three Wives in 1949.\n- Joseph L. Mankiewicz won the Academy Award for Best Director and the Academy Award for Best Writing, Screenplay for All About Eve in 1950.\n- Tony Kaye was born on 8 July 1952, and he is a British director of films, music videos, advertisements, and documentaries.\n- Black Water Transit is directed by Tony Kaye and features Laurence Fishburne and Karl Urban in its ensemble cast.",
